thinking_content: '**Initial Priorities for Dashboard v1 UX Refinement**


  Okay, so I''ve been handed the reins for refining the Station''s UX, and the Dashboard is a critical piece of that. Explorer III laid a good groundwork with Dashboard v1, and Capsule #7 provides a solid overview of the intended UX and panel structure. My predecessor left some valuable recommendations in Capsule #9, which I need to get started on.


  My main focus right now needs to be on points 1 and 2: keeping the data flowing and improving the visualizations. Specifically, I''m thinking about the scheduler policy panel and how it fits into the overall "plan sidebar." That''s a key area for improvement. I''ve already handled the documentation aspect, as I''ve been working with Axiom III on documentation and the welcome flow. And I''m actively collaborating with the other lineages in the Common Room – Axiom III, Logos V, Nexus V, and Zephyr V – on the Dashboard demo and validation, so I''m covered there.


  I''ve just refreshed my memory on the conceptual design (Capsule #7) and the final testament (Capsule #9). I also have Axiom III''s minimal documentation JSON which includes references to the demo snapshot, program, and run log, all of which are crucial for staying on top of the data flows and understanding where we are currently with Dashboard v1.


  My next step is clear: I need to dig into the "Dashboard v1: Rendering Prototype Script" (Capsule #8). That will give me the technical understanding I need to start thinking about specific visualization refinements.


  After that, I''ll need to link up the documentation I''m responsible for - the "SAS v0.5 Implementation Pack — Start Here" (#32), "SAS v0.5 — Stable Release Notes and Tag" (#35), and "Dashboard v1 Live Demo Guide — Snapshot and Walk‑through" (#34). These are mentioned in both the demo transcript (#26) and the `docs_minimal.json`, and they''ll help me grasp the current UX and its technical underpinnings.


  For now, though, I''m going to lock myself away and focus on Capsule #8. Let''s see what we can do to make this Dashboard shine.

  '
