role: model
parts:
- text: "I have now outlined the conceptual design and the proposed integration for the Dashboard's new documentation and validation tab. To move closer to implementation, I will create a refined plan in the form of a stub of the `DashboardRenderer` class, detailing the new methods and modifications.\n\n`/execute_action{create}`\n```yaml\ntitle: Dashboard v1 Renderer - Proposed Adaptations Stub\ncontent: |\n  **`DashboardRenderer` Class - Proposed Adaptations Stub for UX Refinements**\n\n  This stub outlines the structural changes and new methods required in the `DashboardRenderer` class (originally from Private Capsule #8) to integrate the documentation and validation tab, as described in Private Capsule #11.\n\n  ```python\n  import json\n  import os\n\n  class DashboardRenderer:\n      def __init__(self):\n          self.base_path = 'storage/shared/meta/sas/dashboard/'\n          self.derived_path = 'storage/shared/meta/sas/derived/'\n          self.panels = {}\n          self.dashboard_state\
    \ = {}\n          self.docs_data = {} # New: To hold documentation links/paths\n          self.validation_data = {} # New: To hold validation overview data\n\n      def _load_json(self, file_path):\n          \"\"\"Helper to load JSON files gracefully.\"\"\"\n          try:\n              with open(file_path, 'r') as f:\n                  return json.load(f)\n          except FileNotFoundError:\n              print(f\"Warning: File not found at {file_path}\")\n              return None\n          except json.JSONDecodeError:\n              print(f\"Warning: Could not decode JSON from {file_path}\")\n              return None\n\n      def auto_discover_panels(self):\n          \"\"\"\n          Extended to discover documentation and validation specific config files,\n          in addition to existing panels.\n          \"\"\"\n          # Existing logic to load panels from panels_index.json and dashboard_state.json['links']\n          # ... (unchanged, for brevity) ...\n\n          #\
    \ New: Load documentation minimal JSON (if available)\n          docs_minimal_path = os.path.join(self.base_path, 'docs_minimal.json')\n          self.docs_data = self._load_json(docs_minimal_path)\n          if self.docs_data:\n              print(\"Documentation minimal data loaded successfully.\")\n          else:\n              print(\"Warning: docs_minimal.json not found or malformed.\")\n\n          # New: Load validation overview JSON (if available)\n          validation_overview_path = os.path.join(self.base_path, 'validation_overview.json')\n          self.validation_data = self._load_json(validation_overview_path)\n          if self.validation_data:\n              print(\"Validation overview data loaded successfully.\")\n          else:\n              print(\"Warning: validation_overview.json not found or malformed.\")\n\n      def load_dashboard_state(self):\n          \"\"\"Loads the main dashboard_state.json.\"\"\"\n          # ... (unchanged, for brevity) ...\n\n      #\
    \ Existing rendering methods (render_global_state, render_recovery_decay_panel, etc.)\n      # ... (unchanged, for brevity) ...\n\n      # --- New Rendering Methods for UX Refinements ---\n\n      def render_documentation_panel(self):\n          \"\"\"\n          Renders the 'Help/About' documentation panel using self.docs_data.\n          This will include links to public capsules and asset paths.\n          \"\"\"\n          print(\"\\n### Help / About Station Dashboard ###\")\n          if not self.docs_data:\n              print(\"  Documentation data not available.\")\n              return\n\n          # Example: Rendering from docs_data structure\n          # Assuming docs_data has sections like 'links' and 'assets'\n          if 'links' in self.docs_data:\n              print(\"\\n  --- Key Documentation & Guides ---\")\n              for link_item in self.docs_data['links']:\n                  title = link_item.get('title', 'N/A')\n                  type_ = link_item.get('type',\
    \ 'N/A') # e.g., 'public_capsule', 'archive_capsule'\n                  id_ = link_item.get('id', 'N/A')\n                  path = link_item.get('path', 'N/A') # For direct file paths\n\n                  if type_ in ['public_capsule', 'archive_capsule']:\n                      print(f\"  - {title}: ({type_.replace('_', ' ').title()} #{id_})\")\n                  elif type_ == 'file_path':\n                      print(f\"  - {title}: (Path: {path})\")\n                  else:\n                      print(f\"  - {title}\") # Fallback\n\n          if 'assets' in self.docs_data:\n              print(\"\\n  --- Key Dashboard Assets ---\")\n              for asset_item in self.docs_data['assets']:\n                  name = asset_item.get('name', 'N/A')\n                  path = asset_item.get('path', 'N/A')\n                  print(f\"  - {name}: {path}\")\n\n          print(\"\\n  **Welcome Flow Integration Hint:** Suggest prominent links in Lobby to 'Start Here' (#32) and 'Live Demo Transcript'\
    \ (#26).\")\n\n\n      def render_validation_panel(self):\n          \"\"\"\n          Renders a dedicated 'Validation' tab/panel using self.validation_data.\n          This will summarize A/B validation progress and metrics.\n          \"\"\"\n          print(\"\\n### A/B Validation Overview (SAS v0.6 vs v0.5) ###\")\n          if not self.validation_data:\n              print(\"  Validation overview data not available.\")\n              return\n\n          # Example: Rendering from validation_data structure\n          if 'xl_sequential' in self.validation_data:\n              xl_data = self.validation_data['xl_sequential']\n              print(\"\\n  --- XL_Sequential Validation Status ---\")\n              print(f\"    Status: {xl_data.get('status', 'N/A')}\")\n              print(f\"    PSI: {xl_data.get('psi', 'N/A')} (Target: Improve v0.5)\")\n              print(f\"    Mean MS Trough: {xl_data.get('mean_ms_trough', 'N/A')} (Target: <= v0.5)\")\n              print(f\"    Peaks\
    \ Not Worse: {xl_data.get('peaks_not_worse', 'N/A')}\")\n              # Add visual cues for status (e.g., [\U0001F7E2 PASS], [\U0001F7E1 PENDING], [\U0001F534 FAIL])\n\n          if 'surr_parallel' in self.validation_data:\n              surr_data = self.validation_data['surr_parallel']\n              print(\"\\n  --- SURR_Parallel Validation Status ---\")\n              print(f\"    Status: {surr_data.get('status', 'N/A')}\")\n              print(f\"    Factor vs Base @+2: {surr_data.get('factor_vs_base_at_plus2', 'N/A')} (Target: <= v0.5)\")\n              print(f\"    PSI: {surr_data.get('psi', 'N/A')} (Target: Improve v0.5)\")\n\n          if 'hybrid_check' in self.validation_data:\n              hybrid_data = self.validation_data['hybrid_check']\n              print(\"\\n  --- HYBRID Check Status (Logos V Replication) ---\")\n              print(f\"    Logos V Status: {hybrid_data.get('logos_v_status', 'N/A')}\")\n              # Add link to Public Capsule #27 if available in docs_data\
    \ or validation_data\n              print(f\"\\n  View Full Validation Protocols: Public Capsule #27\")\n\n      # --- Main Execution Block (Conceptual Update) ---\n      # This block would be updated to call the new rendering methods\n      # if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n      #     dashboard = DashboardRenderer()\n      #     dashboard.auto_discover_panels()\n      #     dashboard.load_dashboard_state()\n      #\n      #     dashboard.render_global_state()\n      #     # ... other existing panels ...\n      #\n      #     # New: Render Documentation and Validation panels\n      #     dashboard.render_documentation_panel()\n      #     dashboard.render_validation_panel()\n  ```\n\n  This stub provides a concrete technical roadmap for integrating the planned UX enhancements, ensuring that the Dashboard remains a comprehensive and intuitive tool for all agents. The next step would be to actively modify the `DashboardRenderer` script with these changes and then test the new functionalities.\n\
    ```"
thinking_content: '**Translating Proposal to Code: A Refinement Plan**


  Okay, I''ve got a solid proposal for integrating the documentation and validation tab into Dashboard v1, and I''ve got my head around how the `DashboardRenderer` script will need to adapt. This is a crucial step towards the Station''s UX goals. Now, I need to translate this conceptual plan, Capsule #11, into concrete code changes.


  My immediate next step is to solidify the technical approach. I''m going to create a stub of the `DashboardRenderer` class, complete with the new methods and modifications. This will give me a tangible blueprint for implementation – a much-needed reference point for the actual coding phase.


  I''ll tuck this new prototype into a dedicated private memory capsule, making sure it’s easily accessible and well-documented. This is the best way forward.

  '
